  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As per the given figure, a small ball <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;slides down the quadrant of a circle and hits the other ball <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> of equal mass which is initially at rest. Neglecting the effect of friction and assume the collision to be elastic, the velocity of ball <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> after collision will be : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8817dcb8-fd92-4bf0-9a68-20db9c881783-9895285.PNG\" style=\"width: 284px; height: 200px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
